/-!
# The residue field at a point of a blowup

A sequence of blowups at closed points in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupSequence` requires the residue field at the centre to be unchanged
from one stage to the next: the field `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_residue` of a rule
for choosing the centres asks that `Scheme.Hom.residueFieldMap` of the blowup morphism at the
chosen point be an isomorphism. This file supplies the two halves of that condition which the
project can prove.

The first half is general and formal. A morphism of residue fields is a homomorphism of fields,
hence injective, so it is an isomorphism exactly when it is surjective; and surjectivity can be
tested on the stalk map, or on the sections over an affine open containing the image point. So
`next_residue` at a point `q` of the blowup over `p` is exactly the statement that the residue
field at `q` is generated by the residue field at `p` — that `q` is a rational point of the
fibre.

The second half is the Claim of Section 54.12 of the source, which is where that rationality
comes from for a rational double point: in case I an ideal `I ⊆ κ[y₂, y₃]` whose square contains
the dehomogenized quadratic form has colength at most one, and a `κ`-algebra of rank at most one
is `κ`. So the singular points of the exceptional curve are `κ`-rational.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_iff_surjective`: a residue field map is an isomorphism
  exactly when it is surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_stalkMap_residue` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_residueFieldMap_of_surjective_germ_residue`: surjectivity tested on
  the stalk map, and on the sections over an open containing the image point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bijective_algebraMap_of_rank_le_one`: a nontrivial algebra of rank at most
  one over a field is that field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bijective_algebraMap_quotient_of_not_isScalarSqLinear`: **the residue field
  at a singular point of the exceptional curve in case I is `κ`.**

## Implementation notes

What is still missing for `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_residue`. Two steps separate
`AlgebraicGeometry.bijective_algebraMap_quotient_of_not_isScalarSqLinear` from it, and both are
the same step that blocks `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupStep.next_exceptional`. First, the
singular closed point of the blowup lying over the centre has to be known to lie in the standard
affine chart attached to a good coordinate `x₁`, so that the identification
`AlgebraicGeometry.chartQuotientEquivQuadric` of `A[𝔪/x₁]/x₁A[𝔪/x₁]` with
`κ[y₂, y₃]/(q(1, y₂, y₃))` applies to it and turns it into an ideal `I` of `κ[y₂, y₃]`. Second,
singularity of the blowup at that point has to be converted into `q(1, y₂, y₃) ∈ I²`, the
hypothesis `hmem` below. So the two conditions `next_exceptional` and `next_residue` of a rule
are blocked on one and the same pair of steps.

The third step the source takes, moving the singular point of the blowup to the origin of the
first chart so that `ā₁₁ = ā₁₂ = ā₁₃ = 0`, is no longer missing: it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isGoodCoordinateForm_of_dehomogenized_mem_sq` in the sibling module
`ChartNormalization`, which takes the same `hmem` as `hcase` here and produces generators of the
maximal ideal whose first one is a good coordinate. The existence of a good coordinate is
therefore not conditional on that vanishing any more; the vanishing is a conclusion.

Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` attribute. The general lemmas are formal facts about
`Scheme.Hom.residueFieldMap`, and the Claim is registered where it is proved, in
`RationalDoublePoints/CaseDichotomy.lean`, whose hypotheses on the quadratic form are the
source's case I rather than any tag's setup.

